  "aiContextParagraph": "The Indonesian House of Representatives (DPR) halted impeachment proceedings against the Vice President after he officially stepped down from his post. Following this development, public attention has shifted toward the legitimacy of educational credentials within the government. A petition has garnered significant support, requesting the General Election Commission (KPU) to verify the diplomas of all legislative members. The KPU responded by confirming that all sitting members of the House of Representatives have successfully fulfilled the minimum educational requirements mandated by law. Legislative leadership and relevant committees have engaged in discussions regarding these transparency demands, while the House continues to conduct its regular plenary sessions. This sequence of events follows the resignation of the Vice President, which rendered the previously scheduled impeachment vote unnecessary.",
